# The walk trusts a signature that says `fresh`: what it remembers about such an object survives calls to other code.
# The injected fault marks Array.prototype.reverse as fresh, although it returns its receiver.
# A release build then prints a wrong answer and does not stop. The proof checks and the freshness check each stop the program.
# AS-USERS-BUILD: a build with assertions always runs the freshness check, so it cannot show the silent wrong answer
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: 4,1
# CHECK-NEXT: went on
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(FAULT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Array.prototype.reverse/FreshnessOfResult
# FAULT: 4,4
# FAULT-NEXT: went on
# FAULT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(PROOFS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Array.prototype.reverse/FreshnessOfResult,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# PROOFS: a load or check that the compiler removed as redundant gives a different result here
# PROOFS-NOT: went on
# PROOFS: crashed
# RUN(FRESHNESS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Array.prototype.reverse/FreshnessOfResult,CheckResultFreshnessAtRunTime
# FRESHNESS: bun: internal AOT error: fresh result check failed
# FRESHNESS-NEXT: Array.prototype.reverse is declared to return a fresh object, but the result is the receiver
# FRESHNESS-NOT: went on
# FRESHNESS: crashed
